+ * validation. An attacker who controls the serialized byte stream can therefore inject
+ * predicate-violating entries/elements that the constructor and every public mutator would reject,
+ * producing a "split-brain" instance: a {@code Predicated*} typed object whose type contract
+ * guarantees (e.g. "no null keys") are silently violated.</p>
