+ * <p>Each test below crafts an <em>attacker-controlled</em> serialized stream. Because the safe
+ * constructor/factory always calls {@code validate()}, a violating instance cannot be built through
+ * the public API; the harness instead builds a valid instance, then reflectively swaps its backing
+ * map/collection field for one holding a predicate-violating entry BEFORE serializing it. This
+ * faithfully models a hostile serializer that emits {@code predicate=NotNullPredicate} together with
+ * a decorated store containing a null &mdash; exactly the bytes {@code writeObject}/{@code
+ * defaultWriteObject} produce for such a doctored object, and exactly what an attacker who never runs
